  number       = 1,
  month        = {AUG 20},
  abstract     = {Alloying is an established strategy to tune the
    properties of bulk compounds for desired applications. With the
    advent of nanotechnology, the same strategy can be applied to 2D
    materials for technological applications, like single-layer
    transistors and solid lubricants. Here we present a systematic
    analysis of the phase behaviour of substitutional 2D alloys in the
    Transition Metal Disulfides (TMD) family. The phase behaviour is
    quantified in terms of a metastability metric and benchmarked
    against many-body expansion of the energy landscape. We show how
    the metastability metric can be directly used as starting point
    for setting up rational search strategies in phase space, thus
    allowing for targeted further computational prediction and
    analysis of properties. The results presented here also constitute
    a useful guideline for synthesis of TMDs binary alloys via a range
    of synthesis techniques.},
